    "number": "Theorem 2",
    "quote": "For any sequence of losses $\\ell_t\\in[-1,1]^K$ and any $\\eta<1$, LB-Prod produces valid distributions $\\pi_t\\in\\Delta([K])$ and its regret  is bounded by $\\sum_{t=1}^T \\E[\\ell_{t,A_t} - \\ell_{t,i^*}]\\leq 2+\\frac{K\\log(T)}{\\eta} + \\frac{2\\eta T}{1-\\eta}$."
   },
   "confidence": "medium",
   "notes": "The bound holds for any eta<1 (horizon marked anytime since eta is free; with tuning eta = sqrt(K log T/(2T)), which requires T, the text states O(sqrt(KT log T)) for T > K log(T)/2). The proof actually derives 4*eta*T/(1-eta) rather than 2*eta*T/(1-eta); the statement is recorded as printed."
  },
